  "live_records": {
    "q-73842": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73842",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1$ at the point $(1,1,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1) & =\\frac{1}{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{1}{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) \\\\ z-1 & =1\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ z-1 & =x+y-2 \\\\ -x-y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ x+y-z-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
